    "result_text": "The change is complete and all tests pass.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required assigning a `membershipNumber` formatted `<customerCode>-M<YY>`, where `YY` is the last two digits of the `registrationDate` year (e.g. `SMI-0007-M26`).\n\nSince this is a value fully derived from the owner's own persisted fields (`customerCode` and `registrationDate`), I implemented it as a read-only computed field following the exact pattern already used for `displayName`, `initials`, and `customerCode`:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `membershipNumber` property to the `Owner` schema (which generates the `membershipNumber` field on `OwnerDto` at build time).\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a `@Mapping` for `membershipNumber` plus a `formatMembershipNumber` method that formats it as `String.format(\"%s-M%02d\", customerCode, registrationDate.getYear() % 100)`, returning null when either source field is absent.\n\nThe `%02d` on `year % 100` correctly zero-pads the two-digit year, matching the test's `registrationDate.substring(2, 4)` expectation. The acceptance test `coreMembershipNumberFormat` and the full build both pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).",
